gps.uc: disable GPS when services.gps is not configured

Without services.gps the template wrote nothing, so /etc/config/gps kept
the package default disabled=0. On OAP101 GPS and BLE share /dev/ttyMSM1,
and ucentral-gps then switches the UART to GPS at boot, breaking BLE.
This applies to every board that ships ugps (all ucentral-ap images):
without services.gps, GPS is now off instead of on.

Local patch until the change lands in wlan-ucentral-schema; drop it
when PKG_SOURCE_VERSION is bumped past that commit.

--- a/renderer/templates/services/gps.uc
+++ b/renderer/templates/services/gps.uc
@@ -10,8 +10,23 @@
 
 		services.set_enabled("umdns", enable);
 
-		if (!enable)
-			return '';
+		// No services.gps in the configuration: disable GPS explicitly.
+		// Writing nothing would leave the package default (disabled=0).
+		// On OAP101 GPS and BLE share /dev/ttyMSM1, so GPS-on-by-default
+		// lets ucentral-gps take the UART away from BLE at boot.
+		// Only boards that ship ugps have /etc/config/gps to write to.
+		if (!enable) {
+			if (!services.is_present("ugps"))
+				return '';
+
+			let off = [];
+
+			uci_comment(off, '# generated by gps.uc');
+			uci_comment(off, '### GPS not configured - keep it disabled');
+			uci_set_number(off, 'gps.@gps[-1].disabled', 1);
+
+			return uci_output(off);
+		}
 
 		let output = [];
 
